{
  "_about": "Entries whose ONLY content is a pointer at another regulation — 'See Wahleach Lake', 'Tributary of Slocan River; see Slocan River regs'. Extracted from the prose entries/synopsis corpus before it was retired, so the catalogue reparse can mark the same entries the same way instead of rediscovering them.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: an earlier analysis resolved each single-rule 'See X' stub against the registry and found 24 of them point at THEIR OWN registry item — r2:jones_lake@2-3 is item wbk:329177886, whose registry name is already Wahleach Lake and which already carries the alias WAHLEACH (JONES) L. Those are not rules and not even information; they are an alias the alias table already holds. The rest name a genuinely different water and belong on the entry as a governed_by edge.\n\nkind: water_pointer = names another water · page_pointer = points into synopsis prose not in this corpus (dangling; flag, do not render as a rule) · program_membership = Youth/Disabled Accompanied Water, which is a real type, not a pointer.\n\nThe prose `details` paraphrase each entry carried was removed 2026-09-23; `verbatim` is the printed text.",
  "source": "data/curated/regulations/entries/synopsis (retired at commit f7679d4)",
